# Confirm = publish to the web

When the user says **confirm** (or "confirm and deploy", "push it", "put it live"):

1. Work in `C:\Users\Tomas\Documents\tomasekplays` (TomasekPlays site → tomasekplays.com via GitHub).
2. Run `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log -5 --oneline`.
3. Stage the relevant site changes (HTML/CSS/JS/assets). Do **not** commit secrets.
4. Commit with a short message about why (HEREDOC / PowerShell here-string).
5. **Push** to `origin main` immediately so the live site updates.
6. Reply with the commit summary and that it is live / pushed.

Do this without asking again once they said confirm.
Only create a commit when they said confirm (or explicitly asked to commit/push/deploy).
